# Copy this file to ".env" and fill it in. NEVER commit your real .env.
#
# --- Authentication (pick ONE approach) ---
#
# Option A (recommended): a read-only app registration. Fill in all three below.
#   The app's own token covers every plane - Graph, Azure, Dataverse, Power Platform -
#   so the audit runs on this one credential with NOTHING interactive and no Azure CLI.
#   The exact least-privilege permissions are in docs/permissions.md.
TENANT_ID=
CLIENT_ID=
CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# Option B: run as yourself (no app). Leave CLIENT_ID / CLIENT_SECRET blank.
#   Graph uses an interactive device-code sign-in (a code + https://microsoft.com/devicelogin
#   link appear; no app, no secret, no module). Azure, Dataverse, and Power Platform use your
#   Azure CLI token, so run `az login` first. That is two sign-ins with the same account.
#   Note: the .Read.All Graph scopes need a one-time admin consent to the app
#   "Microsoft Graph Command Line Tools" before a Global Reader can sign in.
#
# --- Scope ---
#
# Dataverse environments to audit (comma-separated URLs). Leave blank to skip Dataverse.
DATAVERSE_ENVIRONMENTS=https://yourorg.crm.dynamics.com
#
# Azure subscriptions to audit (comma-separated IDs). Leave blank to audit every
# subscription your identity can read.
AZURE_SUBSCRIPTIONS=
